Mitcad patch (mitcad#343): the start of a rounding along an edge of a
face the ball touches at no point goes on across that face.

A notch cut into a ring's outer cylinder left at one corner a strip 5 um
wide of an earlier rounding of radius 0.4 between the notch and the
cylinder; its edge with the notch is rounded with 1. The strip is convex
and bends more sharply than the ball, so no ball inside the solid touches
it: the section on the edge's faces has no solution even on their
surfaces. StartSolOverflow went on across a face only after a side had
moved (a face the ball touches at no point found beyond the spine's
faces) and gave up when the spine's own face was such a face, so the
rounding had no start ("no ball of the radius touches both faces").
Now, at the spine, the side whose face is convex and bends towards the
solid more sharply than the ball (ballTouchesNoPointOf) goes on across the
face's edge the section crosses, within the rounding's size, as such a side
does further on: the ball touches the notch and the cylinder, the strip
consumed, as at the corner without the strip.

